1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,898
Every client walks in saying:

2
00:00:01,918 --> 00:00:02,850
"I need an app."

3
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:03,838
Most of them don't.

4
00:00:03,858 --> 00:00:05,800
They need a spreadsheet that updates itself.

5
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:07,211
Three questions to tell.

6
00:00:07,231 --> 00:00:09,680
The third is where budgets die.

7
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:11,407
One: who uses it?

8
00:00:11,427 --> 00:00:12,782
Customers, maybe an app.

9
00:00:12,802 --> 00:00:14,108
Only your team?

10
00:00:14,128 --> 00:00:15,459
You need an internal tool,

11
00:00:15,479 --> 00:00:16,710
not an App Store listing.

12
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,321
Two: does the same job happen every

13
00:00:19,341 --> 00:00:21,172
day? Copying orders,

14
00:00:21,192 --> 00:00:22,199
pulling reports,

15
00:00:22,219 --> 00:00:23,271
updating stock.

16
00:00:23,384 --> 00:00:24,624
If it repeats,

17
00:00:24,644 --> 00:00:25,870
automate it.

18
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,659
Three: can you draw the whole thing

19
00:00:27,679 --> 00:00:28,744
on one page?

20
00:00:28,764 --> 00:00:29,311
If not,

21
00:00:29,331 --> 00:00:30,100
don't build yet.

22
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:32,349
That's the step people skip,

23
00:00:32,369 --> 00:00:33,930
and where budgets explode.

24
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:36,581
We scope every project on one page

25
00:00:36,601 --> 00:00:38,606
before writing a line of code.

26
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:40,192
Comment SCOPE and I'll send you our

27
00:00:40,212 --> 00:00:40,960
checklist.
